From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 01:12:26 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: Report vblanks from DCP's swap completions

DCP raises no vblank interrupt the AP sees, so the driver had no vblank
support: no vblank counts or timestamps, flip events stamped by guesswork
from the time since the swap, events for commits without a swap faked
5 ms later from a work item, and no next-vblank time, so the atomic
helpers never gave render fences a deadline.

DCP does complete each swap on the frame boundary. On the J713's panel,
600 swaps submitted at random times complete on a 16,666,476 ns grid
within 15 us, and a swap must reach DCP 2.4 ms before its completion to
make the frame; one later than about 2.35 ms makes it but completes up
to 100 us late. Model the grid from the completions, trusting early ones
over late ones, measure its period over about ten seconds of them, and
run a timer on it for vblanks between swaps. Timestamps are placed so the
next vblank start is the latest time a swap still makes the next frame.

Flip events now carry the vblank's count and time, a commit without a
swap sends its event at the next vblank, and the commit tail waits for
the flip, as DCP holds on to the old framebuffers until then.

On the J713: over 2,730 flips at random and swept times, flip events
step their sequence exactly with the frames, and arrive 1.0 ms after
their timestamps, as placed; drmWaitVBlank returns 600 times in a row
one frame apart; and kmscube's legacy page flips, which failed with
EBUSY after the modeset, run at 60 FPS.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
